n. Memory for numbers could affect attention/accuracy.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Weaknesses: regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. So good technical competence, decision quality, but attitude issues (show-off, not open) affect crew cooperation and adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weaknesses: regarded as a know-it-all, has a hot temper. So good reliability, problem solving, but hot temper and know-it-all may affect crew cooperation and communication.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. All have some concerns. Which candidate has the least severe concerns? Let's weigh.\n\nCandidate B: nasty remarks is serious for crew cooperation. Memory for numbers is a technical issue but maybe manageable.\n\nCandidate D: hot temper is serious, know-it-all also.\n\nCandidate C: not open to new ideas, show-off, but strong leadership and anticipation.\n\nCandidate A: egocentric, communication difficulty, not willing to further education.\n\nWhich is most balanced? Perhaps Candidate C has strong technical and decision abilities, leadership, but attitude concerns may be mitigated? Show-off and not open to new ideas could affect crew cooperation. But maybe still best technical fit.\n\nCandidate B has good stress handling and conscientiousness, but nasty remarks is a red flag for crew environment.\n\nI think Candidate C might be strongest overall, despite attitude concerns, because technical competence and anticipation are critical for long-distance flights. However, we need to discuss all candidates eventually.\n\nThus initial recommendation: Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: none yet, but we can say \"Given the current evidence, I would currently recommend Candidate C because...\"\n\nProvide facts: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Also note concerns: regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nExplain implication: strengths align with technical competence, decision quality, stress resilience; concerns affect crew cooperation but may be manageable.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nNow produce output."}
